  "live_records": {
    "q-106752": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106752",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nIII. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although we have a product of an upper triangular matrix on the left and a unit lower triangular matrix on the right, the order of multiplication is not correct (instead, we need a unit lower triangular matrix on the left and an upper triangular matrix on the right).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
