    "q-32608": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32608",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given that  $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -7\\end{aligned}]$ has the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot D \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-32608-a",
